  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "All three completed experiments are multimodal or image-only; we have no RNA-only baseline. config_026 shows image alone is very weak (acc 0.227), while multimodal configs with pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l reach ~0.53, but we cannot yet quantify how much of that performance comes from RNA vs. the image modality and fusion. config_047 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) changes only the model setting from multimodal to rna_only while keeping the same RNA encoder and profile setting as config_013/007, giving a clean single-variable comparison. If RNA alone approaches ~0.50, the image modality adds little and we should focus budget on RNA encoder/aggregation choices; if it is substantially lower (e.g., ~0.35), the image contribution is large and we should invest in better image encoders and fusion. This baseline is the single most informative missing data point for guiding all subsequent design decisions under a tight budget."
}

